# clausal: no-collect
# Final review M-a: the OWNER of `qq/1`.  Its importer
# (`listing_import_user.seam`) must be able to list it by indicator, not
# only by the bare class -- an -import_from binds this class, whose clauses
# live on THIS module's row, so a `db.row("qq", 1)` in the importer's own
# database finds nothing.
-module(listing_import_owner, [qq(X)])

qq(1),
qq(2),
